From: Reinhard Tartler <siretart@tauware.de>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 08:29:11 +0200
Subject: Disable flaky TestHeadCompactionWhileScraping in Debian builds

This test needs three TSDB head compactions to finish within a hard-coded
15s require.Eventually window and spawns five prometheus instances in
parallel. It is timing-sensitive and flaky on slow builders: on the
riscv64 buildd a single compaction of a 12ms block took 7.76s, so fewer
than three compactions completed within the window and the test failed
with "Condition never satisfied". It has also been observed to fail on
the ppc64el debci runner (Debian bug #1145937).

Disable this test unconditionally for Debian builds, matching the
approach used for other flaky integration tests (e.g. TestDelayedCompaction
in patch 0024 and TestQueryLog in patch 0027).

Related upstream flakes: prometheus#17541 (Windows CI) and prometheus#17956.
Fix proposals exist upstream in prometheus#17966 and prometheus#19192; drop
this patch once upstream hardens the test.

Bug: https://github.com/prometheus/prometheus/issues/17956
Bug-Debian: https://bugs.debian.org/1145937
Forwarded: not-needed
---
 cmd/prometheus/main_test.go | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/cmd/prometheus/main_test.go b/cmd/prometheus/main_test.go
index 7886815..6a2788c 100644
--- a/cmd/prometheus/main_test.go
+++ b/cmd/prometheus/main_test.go
@@ -814,6 +814,7 @@ runtime:
 // concurrently with a scrape does not trigger the data race described in
 // https://github.com/prometheus/prometheus/issues/16490.
 func TestHeadCompactionWhileScraping(t *testing.T) {
+	t.Skip("Disabled for Debian build: timing-sensitive and flaky on slow architectures (Closes: #1145937)")
 	t.Parallel()
 
 	// To increase the chance of reproducing the data race
